## Case Studies

- [Wie Rexel ein dezentrales HR-Modell in eine globale Recruiting-Performance-Engine verwandelt hat](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/de/resources/case-studies/wie-rexel-ein-dezentrales-hr-modell-in-eine-globale-recruiting-performance-engine-verwandelt-hat/)
- [How Rexel Turned a Decentralized HR Model Into a Global Recruiting Performance Engine](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/how-rexel-turned-a-decentralized-hr-model-into-a-global-recruiting-performance-engine/) - By unifying its recruiting infrastructure, Rexel did more than modernize its ATS. The company regained control over a critical driver of global per formance: its ability to attract, mobilize, and deploy talent internationally.
- [Expeditors - Lean Resources. Global Footprint. Robust Results.](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/expeditors-lean-resources-global-footprint-robust-results/) - Expeditors is a Fortune 500 logistics company based in Seattle, WA. Despite a team of over 15,000 employees, they operate with no official HR support and a minimal recruiting function. The company was founded with an entrepreneurial model, allowing a lot of autonomy for hiring, compensation and promotion at each of their branch locations. Their selection of a new Talent Acquisition Suite (TAS) was driven by the need to support their hiring managers in the task of talent acquisition without imposing a training or administrative burden on the managers. Partnering with SmartRecruiters provided them with the ability to track candidate flow, collaborate across the organization, and improve the candidate experience throughout the hiring process, all with minimal additional resource allocation.
- [OceanaGold Slashes Time-to-Fill by 65% and Unifies Global Hiring with SmartRecruiters](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/oceanagold-slashes-time-to-fill-by-65-and-unifies-global-hiring-with-smartrecruiters/) - SmartRecruiters’ open, enterprise-grade platform allows OceanaGold to build and maintain a recruitment ecosystem that’s both standardised and adaptable.
- [Automation in Action: Experian Delivers $25K in Annual Cost Savings and Six Sigma–Recognized Process Excellence with SmartRecruiters](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/cost-savings-and-process-excellence/) - When manual hiring processes began limiting scalability and driving unnecessary costs, Experian’s Costa Rica team took decisive action.
- [How KPMG Australia is Redefining Recruitment Through Human- Centred AI](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/how-kpmg-australia-is-redefining-recruitment-through-human-centred-ai/) - As one of Australia’s leading professional services firms, KPMG is embracing transformation on every front, and talent is no exception. With the world of work evolving faster than ever, KPMG’s People & Inclusion team is leading a shift from process-driven hiring to human-centred, AI-ready recruitment where efficiency, compliance, and candidate experience go hand in hand.
- [How Abano Healthcare increased clinician hires by 32% with SmartRecruiters](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/how-abano-healthcare-increased-clinician-hires-by-32-with-smartrecruiters/) - Abano Healt hcare is a leading dental and healthcare group operating across Australia and New Zealand, employing thousands of clinicians and support staff. With a focus on innovation, care, and community, Abano is dedicated to delivering exceptional patient outcomes through empowered people and progressive technology.
- [How Wolt Scaled its Workforce with Volume Hiring in SmartRecruiters](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/how-wolt-scaled-its-workforce-with-volume-hiring-in-smartrecruiters/) - After a $160 million round of funding in 2019, Wolt was tasked with scaling the organization across Europe. Little did they know this would mean increasing headcount 15 times over within three years.
- [CityFibre Hires for Diversity with SmartRecruiters](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/cityfibre-hires-for-diversity-with-smartrecruiters/) - In the race to connect high-speed fibre to 8 million homes in more than 285 cities, towns, and villages, CityFibre has been on a rapid growth curve. The company knew that its aggressive headcount goals combined with an executive-led initiative to promote equal opportunities could open it up to more high-quality talent. However, CityFigure lacked technology and hiring processes that could support hiring for diversity.
- [CityFibre Empowers Internal Mobility with SmartRecruiters Employee Portal](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/cityfibre/) - With the rollout to connect high-speed fibre to 8 million homes in more than 285 cities, towns, and villages nearing completion, CityFibre knew it would need to embark on a new phase of its business journey. After increasing headcount by 80% over two years, the company wanted to facilitate internal mobility and career development for its current employees.
- [How Anglo American Scaled Job Applications for Candidates Who Lack Internet Access](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/anglo-american/) - In South Africa, where Anglo American hires thousands of employees every year, the company can receive as many as 15,000-20,000 paper resumes per week. To hire, recruiters had to physically go through boxes full of CVs and key the information into an ATS.
- [Miller's Health Systems](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/millers-health-systems/) - Hiring is never easy, but in today’s tight talent market, Logan Treaster faces some unique challenges. A Senior Recruiter with significant experience and expertise in healthcare hiring, Logan is responsible for attracting and engaging skilled candidates across multiple markets for three distinct employer brands: Miller’s Health Systems, Theracare and Home Health Solutions.
- [Sana - Increased Hiring Velocity in 6 Months](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/sana-increased-hiring-velocity-in-6-months/) - As a high-growth eCommerce technology provider competing on the global stage, Sana Commerce felt its employer brand needed a dramatic transformation to attract top talent.
- [Nine: Adapting TA processes & technology post $4 billion M&A](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/nine-adapting-ta-processes-technology-post-4-billion-ma/) - When it was announced that Nine was merging with Fairfax Media Limited to become the largest Australian-owned media company, the Talent Acquisition teams at both companies knew major changes were coming, especially when it came to their recruiting technology. Given that both companies had different applicant tracking systems, processes, and integrations, the team had to find a solution that could unify 3 different recruitment modules to operate as one.
- [Equinox - Hiring the best personal trainers for every fitness club](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/equinox-hiring-the-best-personal-trainers-for-every-fitness-club/) - With dozens of upscale luxury fitness clubs across the US – and rapidly expanding into Canada and Europe – Equinox gives its local managers hiring authority to acquire specialized talent as it enters new markets.
- [Tipico - Putting the Odds in Favor of Better Recruiting and Hiring](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/tipico-putting-the-odds-in-favor-of-better-recruiting-and-hiring/) - Putting the odds in favor of better recruiting and hiring. Stronger recruitment marketing with tools & intuitive UX that prioritizes candidate experience.
- [Pluralsight - Builds a Highly Scalable Recruiting Team and Process](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/pluralsight-builds-a-highly-scalable-recruiting-team-and-process/) - Pluralsight, one of the biggest and fastest-growing online education companies on the internet, had meteoric growth plans: increase its employee base by 500% over four years.
- [Gameloft - Hire the world’s best talent in 30 countries? Game on!](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/gameloft-hire-the-worlds-best-talent-in-30-countries-game-on/) - As the world's leading publisher of mobile and video games, Gameloft's products are downloaded by 3 million gamers every day
- [Christian Brothers Automotive - Growing a strong franchise by growing strong teams](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/christian-brothers-automotive-growing-a-strong-franchise-by-growing-strong-teams/) - Mark Carr founded Christian Brothers Automotive Centers in 1982 because he saw a big gap in the automotive repair industry – a lack of honest and trusted resources for repairs and service. “We’ve transformed the way people view the experience of having their cars repaired,” Mark explained. “Our mission is simple – love your neighbor as yourself.”
- [Colliers International Closes more deals with stronger candidates](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/colliers-international-closes-more-deals-with-stronger-candidates/) - As one of the world’s leading commercial real estate firms, Colliers International operates in 66 countries with 10,000 global employees. The Colliers International Australia group includes a team of more than 1700, which has grown more than 40 percent in the last two years.
- [Axel Springer Improves Efficiency with SmartRecruiters Integrations](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/axel-springer-improves-efficiency-with-smartrecruiters-integrations/) - The recruiting team of Axel Springer National Media & Tech GmbH is responsible for recruiting new employees of about 30 subsidiaries within Axel Springer’s national media segment and Axel Springer Holding. To build a more efficient talent acquisition function, the company needed a system that would engage hiring managers and facilitate collaboration across hiring teams by keeping communications related to hires in one place. They also wanted to reduce the administrative burden of integrating with the SAP HCM.
- [How Colliers EMEA Reduced Agency Spending with SmartRecruiters](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/how-colliers-emea-reduced-agency-spending-with-smartrecruiters/) - At Colliers EMEA, each country is responsible for its own talent management. When the company began a search for a new ATS, some offices were more mature in their processes than others. There was no standard tool for tracking job applicants and no easy way to share knowledge and best practices across teams, which meant that both the candidate and recruiter experience varied widely.
- [How Frasers Group Automated High-Volume Hiring at a Human Pace with AI](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/how-frasers-group-automated-high-volume-hiring-at-a-human-pace-with-ai/) - In the fairy tale, "Goldilocks and the Three Bears," Goldilocks tastes three bowls of porridge, sits in three chairs, and tests three beds before choosing the one that's "just right." After choosing SmartRecruiters to replace its outdated hiring system, Frasers set about building out new processes for high-volume retail hiring. The retail group applied the Goldilocks principle of getting the process "just right" to meet the needs of three constituents: hiring managers, HR, and candidates.
- [Catholic Healthcare Doubles Hiring Volume to Care for Australia’s Growing Aged Population](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/catholic-healthcare-doubles-hiring-volume-to-care-for-australias-growing-aged-population/) - Anyone working in healthcare through the pandemic has a story to tell, and Catholic Healthcare is no exception. When the borders closed in Australia, Catholic Healthcare had an outdated applicant tracking system, a decentralized hiring model across its 70 sites, and just three recruiting staff managing the centralized functions of posting job ads and preparing contracts.
- [PACCOR Builds Mature Recruiting Ecosystem in Less Than One Year](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/paccor-builds-mature-recruiting-ecosystem-in-less-than-one-year/) - After growing through acquisition and going through changes in ownership, PACCOR sought to build a mature recruiting function. When Marcel Rütten joined as the Global Director of Talent Acquisition & Employer Branding in 2020, PACCOR had no systems in place for hiring. The company lacked an ATS, hiring guidelines, and a careers page.
- [Indigo: Recruiting Platform Adds Joy to Customer and Employee Experience](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/indigo-recruiting-platform-adds-joy-to-customer-and-employee-experience/) - As Canada’s largest book, gift, and specialty retailer, Indigo operates 89 superstores and 124 smaller stores across all ten provinces and one territory, plus an online store. Headquartered in Toronto, the company employs more than 6,000 people and makes more than 4,000 hires per year, operating under a decentralized hiring model.
- [Asbury Communities Tames High-Volume Hiring Complexity](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/asbury-communities-tames-high-volume-hiring-complexity/) - Like many non-profit organizations serving older adults with community and care in the United States, Asbury has depended on a decentralized hiring process to staff its network of senior living, outpatient therapy, and pharmacy services for most of its century-long history. But the global pandemic, followed by a skyrocketing requisition load and volatile talent landscape, proved too much for the non-profit’s legacy approach to talent acquisition
- [reBuy: Excellence in recruiting technology today, plus a promising vision for tomorrow.](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/rebuy-excellence-in-recruiting-technology-today-plus-a-promising-vision-for-tomorrow/) - When Bastian Müller joined reBuy reCommerce as HR manager in 2016, his mission was to create a modern recruiting team to attract the high-quality technology and marketing talent the company needed to continue its substantial growth. Part of his challenge included adopting new recruiting technology to achieve hiring success to support that growth – and selected SmartRecruiters because it not only would meet his needs today, but was well positioned to meet future needs as the company continues to grow.
- [Doka Group: How one small core team deployed advanced recruiting technology across 70 countries worldwide](https://www.smartrecruiters.com/resources/case-studies/doka-group-how-one-small-core-team-deployed-advanced-recruiting-technology-across-70-countries-worldwide/)

